-in-florida-phones-switched-off-not-in-ice-custody/articleshow/130448790.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/very-suspicious-two-bangladeshi-students-missing-for-days-in-florida-phones-switched-off-not-in-ice-custody/articleshow/130448790.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-22T23:15:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-130449006,imgsize-71502.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Will Iran play at the 2026 World Cup? Government responds after FIFA president says team will attend]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/130446585.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Iran have qualified for the 2026 FIFA World Cup, but their participation remains uncertain due to security concerns over playing in the United States. FIFA, led by Gianni Infantino, insists matches will proceed as scheduled. Iran’s government is still reviewing the situation, meaning a final decision on whether the team will travel has yet to be made.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/international-sports/will-iran-play-at-the-2026-world-cup-government-responds-after-fifa-president-says-team-will-attend/articleshow/130446585.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/international-sports/will-iran-play-at-the-2026-world-cup-government-responds-after-fifa-president-says-team-will-attend/articleshow/130446585.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-22T22:47:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-130448139,imgsize-757509.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[FBI’s rare Cuba mission: Agents fly to Cuba to recover a child from a transgender parent who wanted transition surgery for child]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/130447100.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An unusual FBI operation saw a US government aircraft fly to Cuba to recover a 10-year-old child from Utah in an international parental kidnapping case. The child's transgender parent and partner are accused of taking the child abroad, allegedly for gender transition surgery. Cuban authorities assisted in the child's safe return.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/fbis-rare-cuba-mission-agents-fly-to-cuba-to-recover-a-child-from-a-transgender-parent-who-wanted-transition-surgery-for-child/articleshow/130447100.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/fbis-rare-cuba-mission-agents-fly-to-cuba-to-recover-a-child-from-a-transgender-parent-who-wanted-transition-surgery-for-child/articleshow/130447100.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-22T22:13:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-130447264,imgsize-1099978.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Top 10 deepest caves in the world: From Veryovkina Cave in Georgia to Sistema Huautla in Mexico]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/130446784.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/top-10-deepest-caves-in-the-world-from-veryovkina-cave-in-georgia-to-sistema-huautla-in-mexico/articleshow/130446784.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/top-10-deepest-caves-in-the-world-from-veryovkina-cave-in-georgia-to-sistema-huautla-in-mexico/articleshow/130446784.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-23T01:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:c